+# Statement of facts — Delgado v. Summit Ridge Hospitality, LLC (No. 25-cv-0442, fictional)
+
+_From working chronology v2 · Posture A; excluded 1 privileged-flagged, 2 undated/unparseable entries._
+
+### 2020-03-03 (day) — hire ⚪
+
+Delgado was hired as a floor manager at the Summit Ridge lodge.
+
+Sources (merged from F2):
+1. Complaint (filed Feb. 6, 2025), ¶ 7 — "Plaintiff was hired as a floor manager on March 3, 2020."
+2. Answer and Affirmative Defenses, ¶ 2 — "Defendant admits Plaintiff was hired as a floor manager on March 3, 2020."
+
+### 2024-12-01 (day) — warning 🔴
+
+Delgado never received any written or verbal warning during her employment.
+
+Source: Declaration of M. Delgado (Feb. 3, 2025), ¶ 11 — "No one ever gave me a written or verbal warning in almost five years."
+
+### 2025-01 (month) — final-wages 🔴
+
+Summit Ridge paid Delgado's final wages by check on January 15, 2025, omitting accrued vacation pay.
+
+Source: Complaint (filed Feb. 6, 2025), ¶ 19 — "Defendant issued final wages on January 15, 2025, but did not include accrued vacation pay."
+
+### 2025-01-09 (day) — termination 🔴
+
+Reyes told Delgado her employment was terminated at the end of the shift.
+
+Source: Complaint (filed Feb. 6, 2025), ¶ 14 — "On January 9, 2025, Mr. Reyes told Ms. Delgado she was terminated, effective at the end of her shift."
+
+### 2025-01-10 (day) — termination 🔴
+
+Delgado's employment was terminated by letter dated January 10, 2025.
+
+Source: Termination letter (Jan. 10, 2025), p. 1 — "This letter confirms the termination of your employment, effective January 10, 2025."
+
+### 2025-02-06 (day) ⚪
+
+Delgado filed this action alleging wrongful termination and unpaid wages. [SME VERIFY]
+
+Source: Complaint (filed Feb. 6, 2025), ¶ 1 — "Plaintiff files this Complaint on February 6, 2025."
